  "headline": "Tony Buys the Dip, Koble Tries to Stop the Bleeding",
  "publicationDraft": "Koble had two injured running backs in Mixon and Montgomery when Tony offered Robinson and Moss. The reinforcements delivered 32.90 points immediately, while Tony could afford to stash Mixon on his bench. The gamble paid off spectacularly: Mixon eventually scored 29.50 in Tony's 4.30-point championship victory over Evans. Koble cut Moss in November, while Robinson endured Jacksonville's coaching circus before tearing his Achilles in Week 16. Koble's emergency depth move made sense; Tony's willingness to absorb short-term injury risk secured the better long-term asset. The championship doesn't make Koble an idiot, but Tony bought a damn good running back at exactly the right moment.",
